## Task Hierarchy

RWP uses a 4-level hierarchy for work decomposition:

```
P-01 (Phase)                    # Top-level phase
P-02 (Phase)                    # Another top-level phase
  └── P-02-A (Sub-phase)        # Optional sub-phase within P-02
  └── P-02-B (Sub-phase)        # Another sub-phase
        └── Task T-02-B-01      # Task within sub-phase (if needed)
              └── MT-001        # Micro-task within task (if needed)
P-03 (Phase)                    # Simple phase without sub-phases
AUDIT                           # Special audit phase
P-04 (Phase)
  └── P-04-A (Sub-phase)
  └── P-04-B (Sub-phase)
```

**When to use sub-phases**:
- Complex phases that exceed ~60 minutes of work
- Work that benefits from crash resilience (each sub-phase ~30 min)
- Logically grouped work that should stay together

**When to skip sub-phases**:
- Simple phases that are naturally ~30-60 min
- Straightforward work with clear single objectives

